    "title": "PROJECT ALPHA V2",
    "body": "A high-performance WASM compiler written in Rust. Optimizes matrix multiplications using SIMD vector instructions. Designed to run client-side in edge environments with zero external dependencies, cutting load-phase heap overhead.",
    "codeSnippet": {
      "title": "matrix_simd.rs",
      "lang": "RUST",
      "content": "fn vectorize_simd(matrix: &Matrix) -> Result<Matrix, Error> {\n    let mut result = Matrix::new(matrix.rows, matrix.cols);\n    for row in 0..matrix.rows {\n        // Run SIMD parallel fma instructions\n        unsafe {\n            simd_fma_row(&matrix[row], &mut result[row]);\n        }\n    }\n    Ok(result)\n}"
    },
